* Models for the 5 V buck (U15 AP64501) simulations.
* Diodes' AP64501 has no published SPICE model. AP64501AVG below is an
* averaged peak-current-mode model built from datasheet numbers; it is
* valid up to roughly fsw/5 (about 100 kHz). Switching ripple is studied
* separately with a switching power stage (ripple.cir).

* rshunt (1 Gohm from every node to ground) stops floating internal nodes
* from stalling the solver; it has no visible effect on the results.
.options method=gear rshunt=1e9

.model SC_UV SW(Ron=1 Roff=1e9 Vt=3.3 Vh=0.2)
.model SC_EN SW(Ron=1 Roff=1e9 Vt=1.135 Vh=0.045)

**************************************************************************
* U15 AP64501, averaged peak-current-mode model. Datasheet numbers used:
*   VFB 0.8 V; error amplifier gm 0.15 mS (Ro assumed 10 Mohm)
*   current-sense gain RT 0.089 V/A (COMP volts per inductor amp)
*   soft-start: 4 uA into CSS, reference = lower of SS and 0.8 V
*   UVLO 3.5 V rising, 3.1 V falling; EN 1.18 V rising, 1.09 V falling
*   HS 45 mOhm, LS 20 mOhm (averaged as D x 45 + (1-D) x 20)
*   HS peak current limit 8 A (applied to the average current)
* The inner current loop is modelled as a 190 kHz (about fsw/3)
* bandwidth loop. This stands in for the sampling double pole of
* peak-current-mode control at fsw/2. Not modelled: PFM at light load,
* spread spectrum, the valley limit, thermal shutdown.
* Pins: VIN, LX (averaged switch node, connect L2 here), VOUT (output
* sense for the inner loop), FB, COMP, SS, EN
**************************************************************************
.subckt AP64501AVG VIN LX VOUT FB COMP SS EN params: VOS=0.5 RT=0.089 GM=0.15m RO=10Meg K=4
Vone one 0 1
Ruv one uvn 1k
Suv uvn 0 VIN 0 SC_UV
Ren one enn 1k
Sen enn 0 EN 0 SC_EN
Bon on 0 V=(V(uvn) < 0.5 && V(enn) < 0.5) ? 1 : 0
* soft-start current source, clamped at 2 V, discharged when off
BSS 0 SS I=V(on)*4u*0.5*(1-tanh((V(SS)-2)*20)) - (1-V(on))*V(SS)/100
* error amplifier (gm type) with output resistance and COMP clamp 0.2-2.5 V
BEA 0 COMP I=V(on)*GM*(min(V(SS),0.8) - V(FB))
REA COMP 0 {RO}
DCL COMP ncl DCLMP
VCL ncl 0 2.5
DCL2 nlo COMP DCLMP
VCL2 nlo 0 0.2
.model DCLMP D(Is=1e-12 N=0.5)
* current command from COMP, limited to 8 A
Bic ic 0 V=min(8, max(0, (V(COMP)-VOS)/RT))
* averaged switch node: the inductor sees K x (ic - IL), a first-order
* current loop with bandwidth K/(2 pi L); clamped between 0 and VIN
Bsw swn 0 V=V(on)*max(0, min(V(VIN), V(VOUT) + K*(V(ic) - I(VSL))))
* averaged conduction loss of the two switches (about 30 mOhm at D = 0.4)
Rsw swn lxs 0.03
VSL lxs LX 0
* input current: D x inductor current
Bin VIN 0 I=I(VSL)*V(swn)/max(V(VIN),1)
.ends
